    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the remainder when a number \\( n \\) is divided by 3, 5, and 15, we can use the information given in the problem statement. According to the problem, when \\( n \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. So, we can express this mathematically as:\n\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\]\n\nThis means that \\( n \\) can be written as:\n\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\n\nwhere \\( k \\) is an integer. We need to find the remainders of \\( n \\) when it is divided by 3 and 5. Let's start with the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3:\n\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\nWhen divided by 3, the term \\( 15k \\) is divisible by 3, so we only need to consider the remainder when dividing 7 by 3. \n\nSince \\( 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\) with a remainder of 1, we have:\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1. This can also be written as:\n\\[ n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. Since \\( n = 15k + 7 \\), we need to look at the remainder when 7 is divided by 5:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ with a remainder of } 2 \\]\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2. This can be written as:\n\\[ n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nThe sum of the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with some Python code to verify the calculations.\n```python\n# Let's take an example integer n that satisfies n ≡ 7 (mod 15)\nn = 7\n\n# Calculate remainders when divided by 3 and 5\nremainder_3 = n % 3\nremainder_5 = n % 5\n\n# Sum of the remainders\nsum_remainders = remainder_3 + remainder_5\nprint(sum_remainders)\n```",
